WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.919
Film Courage:&nbsp; I want to go back….you got
the script to Rock in a Hard Place (Editor’s

00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:06.759
Note: the set where this interview is taking
place), you came on set, James Cullen Bressack:

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:09.040
…… He saved our a$s is what happened!

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.299
Sheldon A. Smith:…..The director, James!&nbsp;

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:12.700
Great working with you.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.100
James:&nbsp; He literally got the script like
two minutes before…

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.000
I gotta get back to work…He got the script
two minutes before coming on set.&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.670
We had to cast him last minute because somebody
fell out and he ‘killed it!’&nbsp;

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.730
He did a great job.&nbsp;

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.730
He saved us.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.730
Sheldon:&nbsp; Thank you.&nbsp;

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.810
I was rehearsing as I was getting dressed
with Patrick.&nbsp;

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.480
I was rehearsing with the lead actor (Patrick
Muldoon) as I was getting dressed and he was

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.170
like ‘Man, you already know the dialogue?’&nbsp;
and I was like ‘Yeah, I’m trying to pick

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.500
it up’ as I get dressed and go to make-up…I
was crazy.&nbsp;

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.730
They literally just through me in there and
the next thing I know, I’m doing a scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.379
That’s every actor’s dream.

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:44.410
Film Courage:&nbsp; And you said it had been six
months since you’d been in Straight Outta

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.410
Compton?

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.460
Sheldon:&nbsp; Well….no.&nbsp;

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.760
I shot Straight Outta Compton in August 2014,
so a year.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:51.840
Film Courage:&nbsp; A year?&nbsp;

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.140
And you hadn’t booked anything since?

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.140
Sheldon:&nbsp; I hadn’t booked anything.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.480
Film Courage:&nbsp; And this (role) came about
just like that and it was like this is your

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.289
moment.&nbsp;

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:04.050
So when you were taking a Lyft over from wherever
you were staying, what was going through your

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.050
head?&nbsp;

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.050
Were you nervous?

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.050
Sheldon:&nbsp; No.&nbsp;

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.050
I wasn’t nervous.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.370
At first I was thinking like, alright this
pilot probably isn’t anything if someone

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.490
is going to just drop out and not show up.&nbsp;

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:16.480
But I’m going to go because I’m an actor
and I love acting and they’re paying me….so

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.620
I’m going to go.&nbsp;

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.460
And when I got to the set, I was like ‘Oh,
this is the real deal!’

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:26.031
(Laughs) Then I got the jitters and the butterflies
but then I thought about my coach, Bobby Chance

00:01:26.031 --> 00:01:29.410
and you guys have probably seen her work,
you probably know Bobby Chance.&nbsp;

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:34.930
She always tells me just to be a Barracuda,
what ever it is, just pick it up and play.&nbsp;

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:35.930
Have fun.&nbsp;

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.540
Don’t let the dialogue or anything distract
you.&nbsp;

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.750
Just have fun.&nbsp;

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.870
That’s what I did.&nbsp;

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.870
I thought D Major was a fun character and
I was like ‘Oh, this a dream come true.‘&nbsp;

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.360
It’s been a great experience these past
few days.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.140
Film Courage:&nbsp; That’s interesting….be
a Barracuda.&nbsp;

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.460
What is that exactly?&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.111
You said just have fun but is there also an
aggressive side to it where you need to just

00:01:57.111 --> 00:01:58.350
attack things and go after what you want?

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.640
Sheldon:&nbsp; Yeah… you’ve got to just attack
it.&nbsp;

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.132
You’ve got to put your teeth into it, get
a nice grip, and hold on tight.&nbsp;

00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:05.660
And that is just exactly what I did with this
role.&nbsp;

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.129
I put my teeth into it and held on tight.

00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:09.229
Question for the viewers: What tools or tricks
can an actor use to develop a character quickly?

